The electric field vector \mathbf{E}_{2\mathrm{A}} at A due to the negative charge q_2 points towards the right and has the same magnitude. Hence the magnitude of the total electric field E_{\mathrm{A}} at A is
E_{\rm A} = E_{\rm 1A} + E_{\rm 2A} = 7.2 \times 10^4 \,\rm N \, C^{-1}
\mathbf{E}_{A} is directed toward the right.
E_{1B} = \frac{(9 \times 10^{9} \,\mathrm{Nm^{2}C^{-2}}) \times (10^{-8} \,\mathrm{C})}{(0.05 \,\mathrm{m})^{2}} = 3.6 \times 10^{4} \,\mathrm{N} \,\mathrm{C}^{-1}
The electric field vector \mathbf{E}_{2B} at B due to the negative charge q_2 points towards the right and has a magnitude
E_{2B} = \frac{(9 \times 10^{9} \text{Nm}^{2} \text{C}^{-2}) \times (10^{-8} \text{C})}{(0.15 \text{ m})^{2}} = 4 \times 10^{3} \text{ N C}^{-1}
The magnitude of the total electric field at B is
E_{\rm B} = E_{\rm 1B} - E_{\rm 2B} = 3.2 × 104 N C-1 
 E_{\rm B} is directed towards the left.
The magnitude of each electric field vector at point C, due to charge
