It is the change in enthalpy when one mole of a solute is dissolved in a specific amount of a solvent at a constant temperature and under 1 bar pressure. It is also known as integral enthalpy of solution. The amount of solvent is mentioned as its of moles in which one mole of solute is dissolved.
Examples
