M_{2} = \frac{1000 K_{b}W_{2}}{\Delta T_{b}W_{1}}
W_{2} = 50 \text{ g}, W_{1} = 150 \text{ g},
\Delta T_{b} = T_{b} - T_{b}^{0} = 84.27 \text{ }^{0}\text{C} - 77.06 \text{ }^{0}\text{C}
= 7.21 \text{ }^{0}\text{C} = 7.21 \text{ K}
K_b = 2.77 \, {}^{0}\text{C kg mol}^{-1} = 2.77 \, \text{K kg mol}^{-1}
Substitution of these in above equation
M_2 = \frac{1000 \text{ g Kg}^{-1} \times 2.77 \text{ K kg mol}^{-1} \times 50 \text{ g}}{7.21 \text{ K} \times 150 \text{ g}}= 128 \text{ g mol}^{-1}
