The concept of Lorentz force can be easily extended to current carrying conductors placed in uniform magnetic field B. Suppose that the magnetic field is parallel to the plane of paper and a conductor of length \Delta \ell carrying current I is placed normal to the field. Suppose further that the current is flowing downward with a drift velocity \mathbf{v}_d and hence each free electron constituting the current experiences a Lorentz force \mathbf{F} = e \ \mathbf{v}_d \cdot \mathbf{B}
If there are N free electrons in the conductor, the net force on it is given by
