The direction of the force is again given by Fleming's left hand rule.
Eqn. (18.12) can be used to define the unit of magnetic field in terms of the force experience by a current carrying conductor. By rearranging terms, we can write
B = \frac{F}{I\Delta\ell}
Since F is taken in newton, I in ampere and \Delta \ell in metre, the unit of B will be NA&lt;sup&gt;-1&lt;/sup&gt; m&lt;sup&gt;-1&lt;/sup&gt;. It is called tesla (T).

